<mxCell id="r520" value="fib(4) asks for fib(3) and fib(2); each of those asks again until n ≤ 1 (green base cases)" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="370" width="420" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="r521" value="&lt;b&gt;Recurrence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;fib(n) = fib(n − 1) + fib(n − 2)&lt;br&gt;fib(0) = 0, fib(1) = 1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="520" y="120" width="330" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="r522" value="Derive the answer by splitting the big case. The tree shows the cost: fib(2) is solved twice and fib(1) three times." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="520" y="210" width="330" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="r523" value="fib(10) = 55" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontSize=13;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="520" y="280" width="330" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="r524" value="Naive top-down recursion repeats work. Memoization keeps the same shape and solves each subproblem once." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="420" width="820" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
